# StudyFlow: Web App → Android Mobile Conversion

## Background

The web App ([App/](file:///d:/SECURE/000001Studyflowproject/App/src/App.jsx#15-85)) is a polished React+Vite dashboard with 8 screens, dark mode, bilingual i18n (EN/ID), and Firebase Firestore as the data layer. The existing Mobile app (`Mobile/`) is a Kotlin+Jetpack Compose project that has authentication, task/class CRUD, and basic Material3 UI — but the design is very different from the web App and everything is crammed into a single 2000-line [MainActivity.kt](file:///d:/SECURE/000001Studyflowproject/Mobile/app/src/main/java/com/studyflow/nativeapp/MainActivity.kt).

**Goal**: Rewrite the Mobile app's UI to match the web App's design, adapted for a vertical mobile layout. Maintain the same data layer (Firestore direct access with Backend API fallback) and add missing features.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This is a very large project covering **7 complete screen rewrites + architecture restructure + theme + i18n + dark mode**. Due to context limitations, I propose we implement this in **batches across multiple conversations**. This plan covers the full scope, but I recommend we start with **Phase 1-2** (architecture + theme + first 2-3 screens) and continue in follow-up conversations.

> [!WARNING]
> The current Mobile app uses a Backend API ([BackendRepository](file:///d:/SECURE/000001Studyflowproject/Mobile/app/src/main/java/com/studyflow/nativeapp/BackendRepository.kt#31-547)/Retrofit) with Firestore fallback. The web App uses **direct Firestore**. I will keep the existing data architecture (Backend API + Firestore fallback) since it already works and is battle-tested, rather than switching to pure Firestore client SDK.

## Proposed Changes

### Component 1: Project Architecture (Split Monolithic File)

Split the 2000-line [MainActivity.kt](file:///d:/SECURE/000001Studyflowproject/Mobile/app/src/main/java/com/studyflow/nativeapp/MainActivity.kt) into a clean multi-file structure:

```
com/studyflow/app/
├── MainActivity.kt          (entry point, auth state, setContent)
├── theme/
│   ├── Color.kt             (color palette matching web App)
│   ├── Theme.kt             (Material3 theme, dark/light)
│   └── Type.kt              (typography, Inter/Roboto font)
├── navigation/
│   └── AppNavigation.kt     (bottom nav + routes)
├── i18n/
│   └── Translations.kt      (EN/ID strings matching web App)
├── data/
│   ├── BackendApi.kt         (existing, unchanged)
│   ├── BackendRepository.kt  (existing + add calendar/uniforms/sessions)
│   ├── BackendErrorMapper.kt (existing, unchanged)
│   ├── AuthErrorMapper.kt    (existing, unchanged)
│   └── FirebaseInitializer.kt(existing, unchanged)
├── screens/
│   ├── LoginScreen.kt
│   ├── DashboardScreen.kt
│   ├── FocusModeScreen.kt
│   ├── ScheduleScreen.kt
│   ├── CalendarScreen.kt
│   ├── ReportsScreen.kt
│   └── SettingsScreen.kt
└── components/
    ├── StudyFlowCard.kt      (reusable card with dark mode)
    ├── TaskCard.kt
    ├── ClassCard.kt
    ├── TimerWidget.kt
    ├── WeeklyProgressChart.kt
    └── BottomNavBar.kt
```

#### [MODIFY] [MainActivity.kt](file:///d:/SECURE/000001Studyflowproject/Mobile/app/src/main/java/com/studyflow/nativeapp/MainActivity.kt)
- Strip down to only: Firebase init, auth state management, and `setContent { AppNavigation() }`
- Move all composable screens to separate files
- Move business logic to a ViewModel or keep in Activity with delegation

